ollections/dragon-professional/products/dragon-professional-16-annual-subscription",\n      "ctaText": "Buy Annual Subscription",\n      "highlight": true,\n      "features": [\n        "Full Dragon Professional 16 feature set - no limitations",\n        "Install on as many Windows PCs as you need",\n        "$695/yr auto-recurring - save $100 vs one-off annual ($795)",\n        "Enhanced direct support included in subscription price",\n        "Nuance Management Centre (NMC) compatible",\n        "Licence issued as username and password",\n        "Activation may take up to 24 hours after purchase",\n        "Auto-renews annually - cancel before renewal date to stop"\n      ],\n      "faqs": [\n        {\n          "q": "How does the subscription licence work?",\n          "a": "The subscription licence is issued as a username and password rather than a traditional licence key. Activation after purchase can take up to 24 hours. The subscription auto-renews annually at $695 AUD inc GST."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "What is the difference between the $695 auto-recurring and $795 one-off annual?",\n          "a": "The $695 price applies when you set up automatic annual renewal - you save $100 per year compared to the $795 one-off annual option. Both give you the same full Dragon Professional 16 feature set with unlimited PC installs."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Can I install the subscription on multiple computers?",\n          "a": "Yes. Unlike the perpetual licence which allows 2 activations, the subscription licence can be installed on as many Windows PCs as you need."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "What happens if I do not renew?",\n          "a": "If you cancel before the annual renewal date, the licence expires and Dragon Professional will stop functioning. Your user profiles and custom vocabulary are stored locally and will not be deleted."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Is the subscription cheaper long-term than the perpetual licence?",\n          "a": "Over 3 years, the perpetual licence ($994 once) costs less than 3 annual auto-recurring subscriptions ($695 x 3 = $2,085). The subscription suits users who want flexible multi-PC deployment, prefer annual billing, or want to avoid a higher upfront cost."\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "slug": "dragon-professional-16-student",\n      "heroImageKey": "product-student-hero",\n      "featureImageKey": "product-student-feature",\n      "badge": "Student / Education",\n      "navLabel": "Student / Education",\n      "title": "Dragon Professional 16 Student Edition",\n      "metaTitle": "Dragon Professional 16 Student Pricing | $545 AUD | Education | VRA Australia",\n      "metaDesc": "Dragon Professional 16 at student and education pricing. $545 AUD inc GST. Full version, perpetual licence. Two PC activations. For students and educators in Australia.",\n      "headline": "Dragon Professional 16 - Student and Education Pricing",\n      "subheadline": "The complete Dragon Professional 16 experience at a discounted price for students and educators. Dictate essays, assignments, and research faster and more accurately than typing.",\n      "price": "$545",\n      "priceNote": "AUD inc GST - perpetual licence",\n      "licenceNote": "Full version. Licensed per user. Install on up to 2 PCs.",\n      "installLimit": "Up to 2 PCs",\n      "bestFor": "Students and educators",\n      "vraUrl": "https://www.voicerecognition.com.au/cart/add?id=47759915122934&quantity=1",\n      "infoUrl": "https://www.voicerecognition.com.au/collections/dragon-professional/products/dragon-professional-16-educational-student",\n      "ctaText": "Buy Student Edition",\n      "highlight": false,\n      "features": [\n        "Full Dragon Professional 16 - no feature restrictions",\n        "Discounted from $994 to $545 for students and educators",\n        "Perpetual licence - pay once, own it permanently",\n        "Install on up to 2 Windows PCs",\n        "Dictate essays, assignments, and research notes hands-free",\n        "Excellent for students with dyslexia, RSI, or accessibility needs",\n        "Windows 10 and Windows 11 compatible"\n      ],\n      "faqs": [\n        {\n          "q": "Is this the full version of Dragon Professional 16?",\n          "a": "Yes. The student and education edition is the complete Dragon Professional 16 product with no feature restrictions. The only difference is the pricing."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Is proof of student or educator status required?",\n          "a": "Please contact Voice Recognition Australia directly when purchasing for specific eligibility requirements."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Can students use Dragon for accessibility purposes?",\n          "a": "Yes. Dragon Professional is widely used by students with dyslexia, repetitive strain injuries, and other conditions that make typing difficult or painful. Full hands-free PC control is included."\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "slug": "dragon-professional-group",\n      "heroImageKey": "product-enterprise-hero",\n      "featureImageKey": "product-enterprise-feature",\n      "badge": "Enterprise and Government",\n      "navLabel": "Enterprise (Group)",\n      "title": "Dragon Professional Group",\n      "metaTitle": "Dragon Professional Group | Enterprise and Government | VRA Australia",\n      "metaDesc": "Dragon Professional Group for enterprise and government. Centralised management via Nuance Management Centre. Volume licensing, SSO, usage reporting. Contact Voice Recognition Australia.",\n      "headline": "Dragon Professional Group - Enterprise and Government",\n      "subheadline": "Dragon Professional Group delivers the full Dragon Professional 16 capability with added tools for IT teams - centralised management, volume licensing, Active Directory and SSO authentication, and usage reporting via the Nuance Management Centre.",\n      "price": "Enquire",\n      "priceNote": "Volume pricing - contact us",\n      "licenceNote": "Centralised management via Nuance Management Centre. Volume licensing available.",\n      "installLimit": "Managed via NMC",\n      "bestFor": "Teams of 5 or more",\n      "vraUrl": "https://www.voicerecognition.com.au/pages/dragon-professional-group-enterprise",\n      "infoUrl": "https://www.voicerecognition.com.au/pages/dragon-professional-group-enterprise",\n      "ctaText": "Enquire About Enterprise Licensing",\n      "highlight": false,\n      "features": [\n        "All Dragon Professional 16 features for every user",\n        "Centralised management via Nuance Management Centre (NMC)",\n        "Volume licensing with central assignment and redistribution",\n        "Active Directory and SSO authentication support",\n        "Shared vocabulary, AutoText, and command distribution across users",\n        "Usage reporting at user, group, and enterprise level",\n        "TLS 1.2 secured connection to NMC",\n        "Citrix and Remote Desktop (RDP) deployment supported",\n        "Local Australian deployment support from Voice Recognition Australia"\n      ],\n      "faqs": [\n        {\n          "q": "What is the Nuance Management Centre?",\n          "a": "The Nuance Management Centre (NMC) is a server-based administration tool for IT teams to centrally manage Dragon Professional Group deployments - including assigning licences, managing user profiles, distributing custom vocabulary and commands, and monitoring usage across the organisation."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Does Dragon Professional Group support Single Sign-On?",\n          "a": "Yes. Dragon Professional Group supports Active Directory authentication and native NMC authentication. Single sign-on via Windows credentials is supported in managed environments."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "Can Dragon Professional Group be deployed on Citrix or Remote Desktop?",\n          "a": "Yes. Dragon Professional Group supports Citrix and Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) deployments. Specific configuration requirements apply - contact our team for guidance on your environment."\n        },\n        {\n          "q": "What are the security considerations for enterprise deployment?",\n          "a": "Dragon Professional Group communicates with NMC via TLS 1.2. Note that Dragon dictation recording files (DRA files) are not encrypted and should be stored with appropriate security controls. Consult the enterprise installation guide for full security guidance."\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  "benefits": [\n    {\n      "title": "Works offline after activation",\n      "body": "Once installed and activated, Dragon Professional 16 runs without an internet connection. No cloud processing, no data leaving your network. Critical for legal, healthcare, and government users with data handling requirements."\n    },\n    {\n      "title": "Professional accuracy and custom vocabulary",\n      "body": "Dragon Professional 16 adapts to your voice, accent, and industry vocabulary. Add custom words, AutoText shortcuts, and voice macros to build a dictation environment tailored to how you actually work."\n    },\n    {\n      "title": "Transcribe audio recordings",\n      "body": "Beyond live dictation, Dragon Professional 16 can transcribe pre-recorded single-speaker audio files. Supported formats include MP3, WAV, WMA, DS2, and DSS - ideal for field notes and recorded dictation workflows."\n    },\n    {\n      "title": "Enterprise-ready deployment",\n      "body": "Dragon Professional Group adds centralised management via the Nuance Management Centre - volume licensing, Active Directory authentication, shared vocabularies, usage reporting, and Citrix support for large-scale rollouts."\n    }\n  ],\n  "proofPoints": [\n    "40 years in market - trusted by professionals since 1985",\n    "15 million users worldwide across legal, medical, and government",\n    "Works offline after installation and activation",\n    "Local Australian support from Voice Recognition Australia"\n  ],\n  "steps": [\n    {\n      "title": "Choose your version",\n      "text": "Compare perpetual, upgrade, subscription, student, and enterprise options to find the right fit for your needs and budget."\n    },\n    {\n      "title": "Purchase from VRA",\n      "text": "Buy securely from Voice Recognition Australia, Australia's longest-serving Dragon reseller. Receive your licence and download link promptly."\n    },\n    {\n      "title": "Install and start dictating",\n      "text": "Follow the guided installation, activate your licence, and begin dictating immediately. Local support available if you need assistance."\n    }\n  ],\n  "faqs": [\n    {\n      "q": "Is Dragon Professional 16 available for Mac?",\n      "a": "Dragon Professional 16 is a Windows-only product (Windows 10 and Windows 11). There is no Mac version of Dragon Professional 16. Nuance discontinued Dragon for Mac."\n    },\n    {\n      "q": "What is the difference between Dragon Professional 16 and Dragon Professional Anywhere?",\n      "a": "Dragon Professional 16 is a locally installed Windows application that can operate offline after activation. Dragon Professional Anywhere is a cloud-native product that requires an internet connection. Dragon Professional 16 is preferred where data handling requirements or intermittent connectivity are a concern."\n    },\n    {\n      "q": "Can Dragon Professional 16 transcribe meetings or multi-speaker recordings?",\n      "a": "No. Dragon Professional 16 is designed for single-speaker audio only. It will not reliably transcribe multi-speaker conversations, interviews, or meeting recordings. Supported formats for single-speaker transcription include MP3, WAV, WMA, DS2, and DSS."\n    },\n    {\n      "q": "Does Dragon Professional 16 work with Microsoft Teams?",\n      "a": "Dragon Professional 16 includes support for dictating into Microsoft Teams. Some advanced voice commands may have limitations in Teams Home edition. Refer to the Dragon Professional 16 release notes for current Teams compatibility details."\n    },\n    {\n      "q": "Is there a free trial available?",\n      "a": "A 15-day trial is available. Contact Voice Recognition Australia to arrange trial access along with local onboarding support."\n    },\n    {\n      "q": "Which microphone should I use with Dragon Professional 16?",\n      "a": "Dragon Professional 16 works with a range of USB and 3.5mm microphones. Apple AirPods are not supported for dictation. A dedicated dictation microphone or USB headset generally provides the best accuracy. Contact our team for microphone recommendations."\n    }\n  ],\n  "footerLinks": [\n    { "label": "About", "url": "/about" },\n    { "label": "Privacy Policy", "url": "/privacy" },\n    { "label": "Terms", "url": "/terms" },\n    { "label": "Contact", "url": "#final-cta" }\n  ]\n}\n